<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"><head><meta charSet="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"/><link rel="preload" as="image" href="/images/ThePoolLab.png"/><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_next/static/css/d071dca61fbb01bf.css" crossorigin="" data-precedence="next"/><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_next/static/css/0fc6c400c3ed5371.css" crossorigin="" data-precedence="next"/><link rel="preload" as="script" fetchPriority="low" href="/_next/static/chunks/webpack-9104c05f1a1687bc.js" crossorigin=""/><script src="/_next/static/chunks/fd9d1056-4dbbcf07a05c3f48.js" async="" crossorigin=""></script><script src="/_next/static/chunks/472-6eced84fcf03e6a3.js" async="" crossorigin=""></script><script src="/_next/static/chunks/main-app-ce281d8555633725.js" async="" crossorigin=""></script><script src="/_next/static/chunks/326-bff252670b7455ef.js" async=""></script><script src="/_next/static/chunks/app/blog/%5Bslug%5D/page-23a4c3f098b125a3.js" async=""></script><script src="/_next/static/chunks/975-95592eb349967368.js" async=""></script><script src="/_next/static/chunks/app/layout-4ee2f436a51b65f2.js" async=""></script><title>Dolphin Nautilus CC Plus vs Nautilus Titan: Which Robotic Pool Cleaner Should You Buy in 2026? - The Pool Lab</title><meta name="description" content="Compare the Dolphin Nautilus CC Plus and Dolphin Nautilus Titan across cleaning performance, smart features, filtration, ease of use, value, and long-term ownership to determine which robotic pool cleaner is the better choice for your pool."/><link rel="canonical" href="https://www.the-pool-lab.com/blog/dolphin-nautilus-cc-plus-vs-nautilus-titan"/><meta property="og:title" content="Dolphin Nautilus CC Plus vs Nautilus Titan: Which Robotic Pool Cleaner Should You Buy in 2026?"/><meta property="og:description" content="Compare the Dolphin Nautilus CC Plus and Dolphin Nautilus Titan across cleaning performance, smart features, filtration, ease of use, value, and long-term ownership to determine which robotic pool cleaner is the better choice for your pool."/><meta property="og:type" content="article"/><meta property="article:published_time" content="2026-06-03"/><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"/><meta name="twitter:title" content="The Pool Lab - Your ultimate guide to Robot Pool Cleaners, reviews, and maintenance tips."/><meta name="twitter:description" content="Your ultimate guide to Robot Pool Cleaners, reviews, and maintenance tips."/><meta name="twitter:image" content="https://www.the-pool-lab.com/images/ThePoolLabOG.png"/><script src="/_next/static/chunks/polyfills-c67a75d1b6f99dc8.js" crossorigin="" noModule=""></script></head><body class="d-flex flex-column min-vh-100"><nav class="navbar navbar-expand-lg navbar-light bg-light"><div class="container"><a class="navbar-brand d-flex align-items-center" href="/"><div style="width:160px;height:90px;position:relative;margin-right:10px"><img src="/images/ThePoolLab.png" alt="The Pool Lab Logo" style="width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:contain"/></div><span class="d-none d-sm-inline">The Pool Lab</span></a><button class="navbar-toggler" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#navbarNav"><span class="navbar-toggler-icon"></span></button><div class="collapse navbar-collapse" id="navbarNav"><ul class="navbar-nav ms-auto"><li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link" href="/">Home</a></li><li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link" href="/reviews">Reviews</a></li><li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link" href="/best-of">Best of</a></li><li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link" href="/guides">Guides</a></li><li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link" href="/about">About</a></li></ul></div></div></nav><main class="flex-grow-1"><div class="container my-5"><nav aria-label="breadcrumb"><ol class="breadcrumb"><li class="breadcrumb-item"><a href="/">Home</a></li><li class="breadcrumb-item active" aria-current="page">Blog</li></ol></nav><article><h1 class="mb-4">Dolphin Nautilus CC Plus vs Nautilus Titan: Which Robotic Pool Cleaner Should You Buy in 2026?</h1><p class="text-muted mb-5">Posted on <!-- -->2026-06-03</p><div class="row"><div class="col-lg-8"><div><h2>Quick Verdict</h2><p>The <strong>Dolphin Nautilus CC Plus</strong> remains one of the best values in robotic pool cleaning. It delivers reliable floor and wall cleaning, simple operation, and proven long-term durability at a lower price point.</p><p>The <strong>Dolphin Nautilus Titan</strong> builds on the CC Plus platform with Wi-Fi connectivity, app control, improved handling, larger filtration capacity, and a lighter design. For pool owners who want modern convenience and easier ownership, the Titan is the more advanced cleaner.</p><p>If value is your priority, buy the CC Plus. If convenience and smart features matter, buy the Titan.</p><h2>At-a-Glance Comparison</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>Nautilus CC Plus</th><th>Nautilus Titan</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Price</td><td>Lower</td><td>Higher</td></tr><tr><td>Pool Size</td><td>Up to 50 ft</td><td>Up to 50 ft</td></tr><tr><td>App Control</td><td>No</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>Wi-Fi Connectivity</td><td>No</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>Wall Climbing</td><td>Excellent</td><td>Excellent</td></tr><tr><td>Waterline Cleaning</td><td>Good</td><td>Better</td></tr><tr><td>Filter Access</td><td>Top Load</td><td>Top Load</td></tr><tr><td>Ease of Removal</td><td>Good</td><td>Excellent</td></tr><tr><td>Best For</td><td>Value-focused buyers</td><td>Feature-focused buyers</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>Cleaning Performance</h2><p>Both cleaners share much of the same Dolphin DNA. They are designed to clean pool floors, climb walls, and remove everyday debris including leaves, dirt, insects, and fine organic matter.</p><p>The CC Plus has earned a reputation for dependable cleaning performance across thousands of residential pools. It uses Dolphin's CleverClean navigation technology to efficiently cover pool surfaces during a standard cleaning cycle.</p><p>The Titan improves on that formula with enhanced mobility and a lighter chassis. In practice, cleaning performance is very similar, but the Titan tends to navigate more smoothly and maintain better coverage along walls and waterlines.</p><p>Winner: <strong>Titan</strong>, but only by a small margin.</p><h2>Smart Features and Connectivity</h2><p>This is where the largest difference exists.</p><p>The Nautilus CC Plus follows a traditional approach. You place it in the pool, press the button, and let it work. It includes a weekly scheduler but does not offer smartphone control.</p><p>The Nautilus Titan adds Wi-Fi connectivity through the MyDolphin Plus app. Owners can start cleaning cycles remotely, schedule cleanings, monitor status, and manage settings directly from their phone.</p><p>For buyers who appreciate smart-home style convenience, the Titan provides a noticeably better ownership experience.</p><p>Winner: <strong>Titan</strong>.</p><h2>Filtration and Debris Handling</h2><p>Both models use top-loading filter systems that are significantly easier to maintain than older bottom-access designs.</p><p>The CC Plus performs very well with normal debris loads. However, many owners eventually purchase optional ultra-fine filters when dealing with dust, pollen, or fine sediment.</p><p>The Titan includes an updated basket design with increased capacity and improved fine-debris handling. For pools that accumulate heavy debris or require frequent cleaning, the larger basket can reduce maintenance frequency.</p><p>Winner: <strong>Titan</strong>.</p><h2>Ease of Ownership</h2><p>Both robots are easy to operate, but the Titan introduces several quality-of-life improvements.</p><p>The redesigned body is lighter, making removal from the pool easier. It also features improved water evacuation when lifted from the water, reducing strain during handling.</p><p>The CC Plus remains simple and dependable, but the Titan feels more refined during everyday use.</p><p>Winner: <strong>Titan</strong>.</p><h2>Long-Term Value</h2><p>The CC Plus continues to be one of the strongest value propositions in robotic pool cleaners. Its lower purchase price and proven reliability make it easy to recommend to most pool owners.</p><p>The Titan provides additional features and convenience, but buyers must decide whether those upgrades justify the higher cost.</p><p>If your primary goal is keeping the pool clean at the lowest practical cost, the CC Plus remains difficult to beat.</p><p>Winner: <strong>CC Plus</strong>.</p><h2>Who Should Buy the Nautilus CC Plus?</h2><ul><li>You want the best balance of price and performance.</li><li>You do not need smartphone control.</li><li>You prefer simple operation.</li><li>You want a proven model with a long track record.</li></ul><h2>Who Should Buy the Nautilus Titan?</h2><ul><li>You want app control and Wi-Fi connectivity.</li><li>You prefer newer technology.</li><li>You want a lighter cleaner that is easier to handle.</li><li>You value convenience more than minimizing purchase cost.</li></ul><h2>Final Recommendation</h2><p>For most pool owners, the <strong>Dolphin Nautilus CC Plus</strong> remains the smarter purchase because it delivers nearly all of the cleaning performance of the Titan at a lower price.</p><p>The <strong>Dolphin Nautilus Titan</strong> is the better premium option for buyers who value app control, easier handling, and a more modern ownership experience.</p><p>If budget matters, choose the CC Plus. If convenience matters, choose the Titan.</p><h2>Related Resources</h2><ul><li><a href='/reviews/Dolphin-Nautilus-CC-Plus'>Dolphin Nautilus CC Plus Review</a></li><li><a href='/reviews/Dolphin-Nautilus-Titan'>Dolphin Nautilus Titan Review</a></li><li><a href='/best-of/overall'>Best Robotic Pool Cleaners</a></li><li><a href='/best-of/value'>Best Value Robotic Pool Cleaners</a></li></ul><h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2><h3>Is the Dolphin Nautilus Titan worth the extra money?</h3><p>For buyers who want Wi-Fi connectivity, app control, and easier handling, yes. For pure cleaning performance, the CC Plus remains the better value.</p><h3>Does the Nautilus Titan clean better than the CC Plus?</h3><p>Cleaning performance is very similar. The Titan offers slightly better navigation and convenience features, but both deliver excellent cleaning results.</p><h3>Can both robots climb walls?</h3><p>Yes. Both the Nautilus CC Plus and Nautilus Titan can climb walls and clean vertical surfaces in most residential pools.</p><h3>Which model is easier to maintain?</h3><p>Both are easy to maintain, but the Titan's larger filter basket and lighter design make routine ownership slightly easier.</p></div><div class="mt-5"><a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href="/reviews">Find Your Perfect Robot</a></div></div></div></article></div></main><footer class="bg-dark text-white text-center py-3 mt-auto"><div class="container"><p class="mb-1">© <!-- -->2026<!-- --> <!-- -->The Pool Lab<!-- -->. All rights reserved.</p><small class="text-white-50">The Pool Lab<!-- --> is a participant in the Amazon Services LLC Associates Program, an affiliate advertising program designed to provide a means for sites to earn advertising fees by advertising and linking to Amazon.com.</small></div></footer><script src="/_next/static/chunks/webpack-9104c05f1a1687bc.js" crossorigin="" async=""></script><script>(self.__next_f=self.__next_f||[]).push([0]);self.__next_f.push([2,null])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"1:HL[\"/_next/static/css/d071dca61fbb01bf.css\",\"style\",{\"crossOrigin\":\"\"}]\n2:HL[\"/_next/static/css/0fc6c400c3ed5371.css\",\"style\",{\"crossOrigin\":\"\"}]\n0:\"$L3\"\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"4:I[3728,[],\"\"]\n6:I[9928,[],\"\"]\n7:I[8326,[\"326\",\"static/chunks/326-bff252670b7455ef.js\",\"308\",\"static/chunks/app/blog/%5Bslug%5D/page-23a4c3f098b125a3.js\"],\"\"]\n8:I[6954,[],\"\"]\n9:I[7264,[],\"\"]\nc:I[5826,[\"326\",\"static/chunks/326-bff252670b7455